### TABLE 1: `city`
**Purpose:** Reference table for 14 Syrian cities where customers are located.

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| city_id | INTEGER (PK) | Unique city identifier |
| city_name | TEXT | Arabic name of the city |
| population | INTEGER | City population |
| estimated_rent | INTEGER | Average monthly rent (currency units) |
| city_rank | INTEGER | Rank by importance/size (1 = highest) |

**SQL Query:**
SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_rows 
FROM city;
SELECT * FROM city;
SELECT MIN(population) AS min_pop,
MAX(population) AS max_pop,
MIN(estimated_rent) AS min_rent, 
MAX(estimated_rent) AS max_rent
FROM city;
```

