### TABLE 3: `customers`
**Purpose:** 497 registered customers linked to cities.

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| customer_id | INTEGER (PK) | Unique customer identifier |
| customer_name | TEXT | Full customer name |
| city_id | INTEGER (FK → city) | City where customer lives |

**SQL Query:**
SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_rows FROM customers;
SELECT * FROM customers LIMIT 8;
SELECT c.city_name, COUNT(cu.customer_id) AS num_customers
FROM customers cu
JOIN city c ON cu.city_id = c.city_id
GROUP BY c.city_name
ORDER BY num_customers DESC;
