### TABLE 4: `sales`
**Purpose:** Transaction records — 10,388 sales over ~2 years.

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| sale_id | INTEGER (PK) | Unique sale identifier |
| sale_date | TEXT | Date of sale (YYYY-MM-DD) |
| product_id | INTEGER (FK → products) | Product sold |
| customer_id | INTEGER (FK → customers) | Customer who bought |
| total | INTEGER | Sale amount (= product price) |
| rating | INTEGER | Customer rating (1–5) 

**SQL Query:**
SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_rows FROM sales;
SELECT MIN(sale_date) AS first_sale, MAX(sale_date) AS last_sale,
       COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id) AS distinct_customers,
       COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) AS distinct_products
FROM sales;
SELECT rating, COUNT(*) AS count,
       ROUND(COUNT(*)*100.0/(SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sales),2) AS pct
FROM sales 
GROUP BY rating 
ORDER BY rating;
SELECT SUBSTR(sale_date,1,4) AS year, COUNT(*) AS transactions, SUM(total) AS revenue
FROM sales GROUP BY year;
```

**Sample Output:**
```
