###  2C — Data Integrity Check

**SQL Query:**
```sql
-- Orphan records check
SELECT COUNT(*) AS orphan_sales_bad_product
FROM sales s LEFT JOIN products p ON s.product_id = p.product_id
WHERE p.product_id IS NULL;

-- Total mismatch check
SELECT s.sale_id, s.total AS sale_total, p.price AS product_price
FROM sales s JOIN products p ON s.product_id = p.product_id
WHERE s.total != p.price LIMIT 5;

-- Invalid ratings
SELECT sale_id, rating FROM sales WHERE rating < 1 OR rating > 5;
```

**Output:**
```
Orphan sales (bad product_id):    0 ✅
Orphan sales (bad customer_id):   0 ✅
Orphan customers (bad city_id):   0 ✅
Total mismatches (total ≠ price): 0 ✅
Invalid ratings (outside 1–5):    0 ✅
Invalid date formats:             0 ✅
Negative/zero values:             0 ✅
```

**Finding:** ✅ **Full referential integrity** — all foreign keys are valid and all business rules are respected.

